      "content": "that makes sense. thanks. it's just hard because even the local news lately feels like it's being used as theater to keep everyone's eyes off what's actually happening in the Pacific. like, the coverage of the recent port strikes here feels way too heavy-handed, almost like it's a choreographed distraction. do you see any patterns in how \"unrelated\" local disruptions might actually be synchronized with larger moves abroad?",
